L000797	    Finally we observe that even if we change the auxiliary state to be a generic quanutm state with the second moment $(\mu_{R},\chi_{R})$ and the first moment $\vecalpha_{R}$, their action on the second moment of the system state does not change.
L000798	    Therefore, adding non-Gaussian or asymmetric resource to the auxiliary state does not help implementing GCOs without free dilations.
L000799	\end{proof}
