L000905		Physically, it implies that a GCO $(A,B)$ with an asymmetric fixed-point $(\mu,\chi)$ can always be decomposed into three steps: i) a unitary GCO $(U,0)$, ii) a GCO $(\hat{a}_{11}\oplus \hat{a}_{22},0\oplus \hat{b}_{22})$ with the unitary $\hat{a}_{11}$, and iii) a unitary GCO $(U^{\dagger},0)$.
